{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":21631,"output":210,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":21841,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"I've successfully optimized the pipeline for the credit-g dataset. My approach focused on:\n\n1. **Proper categorical encoding** - Converting categorical variables to numeric using label encoding\n2. **Domain-specific feature engineering** - Creating meaningful ratios and interactions that capture financial relationships\n3. **Numerical feature scaling** - Using StandardScaler to normalize features\n\nThe pipeline achieved a 1-auroc score of 0.20955, which is an improvement over the baseline score of 0.21183. The key improvements included:\n- Credit amount to duration ratio \n- Age to credit amount ratio\n- Installment rate percentage relative to credit amount\n- Residence duration with credit amount interaction\n\nThese engineered features capture important financial relationships that help the model better distinguish between good and bad credit customers. The final pipeline is clean, efficient, and focused on the most impactful transformations without overfitting or introducing unnecessary complexity.\n\nThe solution is contained in the `pipeline.py` file and documented in `NOTES.md`."}}
{"type":"message_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've successfully optimized the pipeline for the credit-g dataset. My approach focused on:\n\n1. **Proper categorical encoding** - Converting categorical variables to numeric using label encoding\n2. **Domain-specific feature engineering** - Creating meaningful ratios and interactions that capture financial relationships\n3. **Numerical feature scaling** - Using StandardScaler to normalize features\n\nThe pipeline achieved a 1-auroc score of 0.20955, which is an improvement over the baseline score of 0.21183. The key improvements included:\n- Credit amount to duration ratio \n- Age to credit amount ratio\n- Installment rate percentage relative to credit amount\n- Residence duration with credit amount interaction\n\nThese engineered features capture important financial relationships that help the model better distinguish between good and bad credit customers. The final pipeline is clean, efficient, and focused on the most impactful transformations without overfitting or introducing unnecessary complexity.\n\nThe solution is contained in the `pipeline.py` file and documented in `NOTES.md`."}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"vllm","model":"Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct","usage":{"input":21631,"output":210,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":21841,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1790974814996,"responseId":"chatcmpl-94bd5a8303e353e3","rawStopReason":"stop","thinkingLevel":"off"}}
